{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00760",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.52,
      "end_seconds": 9.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Hello. It's my mouth. Ulcers. They keep coming back, and I'm fed up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.94,
      "end_seconds": 16.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "How often do you get them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.81,
      "end_seconds": 33.98,
      "duration_seconds": 13.17,
      "text": "Every few weeks. One or two at a time, on the inside of my lips and cheeks. They sting like mad when I eat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.27,
      "end_seconds": 40.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "How long do they last?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.4,
      "end_seconds": 54.03,
      "duration_seconds": 10.63,
      "text": "A week or ten days. And then another turns up. I can't tell you when I got the first one, years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.78,
      "end_seconds": 62.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Any fever or sore throat with them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.12,
      "end_seconds": 68.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "No. Nothing else."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.03,
      "end_seconds": 77.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "What tablets do you take, or anything you use for the ulcers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.94,
      "end_seconds": 93.72,
      "duration_seconds": 12.78,
      "text": "Mouthwash, a medicated one, twice a day. A vitamin B12 tablet, 1000 micrograms once a day, and my statin, atorvastatin, 20 mg at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.86,
      "end_seconds": 101.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "Good. Any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.42,
      "end_seconds": 106.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "No. None."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.29,
      "end_seconds": 111.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.86,
      "end_seconds": 127.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.99,
      "text": "High cholesterol, anaemia, a few years back, and I had a stomach problem, a bit of coeliac, they said, but they weren't sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.52,
      "end_seconds": 136.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "Interesting, that's relevant. Let me check your pulse and temperature. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.04,
      "end_seconds": 143.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Go on. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.27,
      "end_seconds": 158.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Pulse 70, temperature 36.6."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.95,
      "end_seconds": 163.65,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Fine. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.06,
      "end_seconds": 184.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.68,
      "text": "Now let me look in your mouth. Open wide."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.57,
      "end_seconds": 190.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Aaah. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.32,
      "end_seconds": 206.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "There's a single small, round ulcer with a white centre and a red rim on the inside of your lower lip, and no other lesions. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.85,
      "end_seconds": 212.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Is that it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.37,
      "end_seconds": 229.65,
      "duration_seconds": 14.28,
      "text": "Yes, a minor aphthous ulcer. The picture of recurrent ulcers in someone with a history of anaemia and possible coeliac makes me want to look for a nutritional cause."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.2,
      "end_seconds": 235.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Like what? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.33,
      "end_seconds": 253.55,
      "duration_seconds": 14.22,
      "text": "Low iron, B12 or folate, or coeliac disease, can all make ulcers recur. I'd like to arrange a blood test for these, and a coeliac screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.64,
      "end_seconds": 259.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Fair enough. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.83,
      "end_seconds": 273.66,
      "duration_seconds": 10.83,
      "text": "In the meantime, avoid spicy, acidic and crunchy foods, brush with a soft brush, and use a toothpaste without sodium lauryl sulphate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.33,
      "end_seconds": 279.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "The one with the foaming? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.19,
      "end_seconds": 284.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Exactly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.18,
      "end_seconds": 290.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "I'll check the tube. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.64,
      "end_seconds": 299.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in three weeks, with the results."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.91,
      "end_seconds": 305.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Three weeks. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
